;;; world/regions/underhum.map - The Underhum's thirteen rooms under the bowl,
;;; from the approved map (topics/harkfell-underhum-map, 2026-10-11) and its
;;; Revision 1 (the cistern climb, approved 2026-10-12).
;;;
;;;   x4   x5   x6   x7   x8
;;;   A -  B -  C -  D            y4  the Throat, the niches, the gallery, the stair
;;;   |              |
;;;   E -  F -  G -  H    I       y5  the roots, the slab, the approach, the chamber;
;;;                  |    |           I behind the chamber's east wall
;;;                  K -  J       y6  under the stone (the cistern's top), the Bearers' Rest
;;;                  |    |
;;;                  L -  M       y7  the cistern, the Last Step
;;;
;;; One loop above (the approved descent and climb). Below the chamber, the
;;; optional cistern: the grate in H's floor drops into K; K and L are the
;;; climb down (glide hops over the fissure); M is the payoff, and its air
;;; shaft (J-M, enclosed) rises one way into I; I and J lead back to K. The
;;; only way in is still the heart in the bowl's floor (A north).
;;;
;;; Breaths: B, E, F, I (four of thirteen).
(map
  region: underhum
  origin: (4 4)
  layout:
  ("A-B-C-D  "
   "|     |  "
   "E-F-G-H I"
   "      | |"
   "      K-J"
   "      | |"
   "      L-M")
  rooms:
  ((A "The Throat" "under the heart a throat of dark stone falls away, and the hum you woke to is all around you")
   (B "The Bearers' Shelf" "four empty niches in the wall take a light each as you pass, the colours you carried down: a breath")
   (C "The Gallery of Stones" "a row of old stones stands in the dark, mute on the way down and ringing on the way up")
   (D "The Ringing Stair" "the rising light from below sets you down on old steps at the top of the chamber's wall")
   (E "The Roots of the Hum" "at the bottom of the throat, steps cut by the old people lead east: a breath")
   (F "The Low Door" "a great slab leans against the wall where it once closed the bowl, and you walk under its place: a breath")
   (G "The Approach" "the passage opens and slopes down toward a sound that makes your own hum louder")
   (H "The Underhum" "a hollow too large for your light, a round dark stone in its middle, and the note you have been hearing all along")
   (I "Behind the Wall" "a narrow passage behind the chamber's east wall, where a crack shows the hollow beyond: a breath")
   (K "Under the Stone" "beneath the chamber's floor the great stone's root goes down into an old cistern, and the hum is strongest of anywhere")
   (J "The Bearers' Rest" "four stone benches under a low roof, where the bearers laid down what they carried")
   (L "The Cistern" "the old people's cistern, dry now, its worn ledges stepping down across a fissure into the dark")
   (M "The Last Step" "the bottom of the cistern, where the stone's root ends and the bearers' story is cut into the wall"))
  borders: ((A north)))
